302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (The second stage sees the full replacement of IPCs with edge AI platforms designed specifically for modern machine vision efficiency. For example, platforms such as NVIDIA Jetson typically operate at just 10 to 30 watts \(or up to 130 watts for the AGX Orin\), making them easy to install, affordable to run, and less demanding on power and cooling resources. These improvements translate into simpler installations, lower electricity costs, lighter demands on backup power, and reduced ongoing maintenance.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (Most Industrial PCs process images using software on general-purpose CPUs, while edge AI platforms leverage dedicated  GPU cores and specialized processors. This difference in hardware allows for real-time execution of multiple, complex neural networks that enable sophisticated tasks such as anomaly detection, predictive quality control, and adaptive learning that can easily exceed the capacity of traditional IPCs. Moving from Industrial  PCs to edge AI platforms as the main processing centers is a transition likely to play out in two stages.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (MIPI A-PHY stands out as the connectivity standard best positioned for this future as most major edge AI platforms, including those from NVIDIA, Qualcomm, Ambarella, and Intel, as well as FPGAs from Xilinx \(AMD\) and Altera \(Intel\) already support native CSI-2 inputs. This plug-and-play compatibility allows the VA7000 to provide seamless, direct camera-to-edge AI platform connectivity that removes unnecessary hardware, supports modern centralized architectures, and maximizes both AI performance and system efficiency.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
